<title>BELGIUM: GLAVERBEL SEES H2 96 PROFIT ABOVE H1.</title>
<headline>GLAVERBEL SEES H2 96 PROFIT ABOVE H1.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian glass maker Glaverbel SA said in a statement on Wednesday that due to the economic recovery and its improved financial structure, profit should be higher in the second-half than in the first half.</p>
<p>&quot;The group's operational performance should lead to second-semester profits (extraordinary items not included) higher than those of the first six months,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>First-half group net profit fell to 227 million francs from 261 million in the first half of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
